      "text": "**Calculating values**\n\nI need to do some calculations! First, I want to look at the numbers below 100 that are positive, specifically from 1 to 99. I find that those divisible by 3 amount to 33, and those divisible by 7 make 14. For numbers divisible by both, their least common multiple is 21, and when I calculate how many times that fits into 99, I get 4. Now, using XOR, I can find the result: 33 + 14 - 2 times 4 gives me 39, which is odd. Now, I should use the tool for further calculations."
